WEBVTT

00:00:00.174 --> 00:00:02.744
What if ISRO had as much money as NASA?

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:07.030
India's Mars mission cost about
seventy four million US dollars.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.720
That's less than the budget
of some Hollywood movies.

00:00:09.845 --> 00:00:13.641
NASA's yearly budget is many
times bigger than ISRO's.

00:00:13.641 --> 00:00:15.986
Imagine what ISRO could do with that.

00:00:15.986 --> 00:00:20.516
It could build bigger rockets, send more
astronauts, explore deeper into space,

00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:24.236
and launch many more satellites for
farming, weather and communication.

00:00:24.527 --> 00:00:27.127
India could become a top
space power much faster,

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.097
and compete with the biggest
names in the industry.

00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:32.932
ISRO already does so much with so little.

00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:35.237
So what if ISRO had NASA's budget?

